  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 159 PM EDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nContinued Dry and Mild Conditions:\n\nHigh pressure continues to dominate the weather pattern into the \nthe extended periods with high temps in the 70s and lows in the \n40s. By Sat morning the main ridge will be centered over the New \nEngland states with its axis angled SW down the eastern seaboard \nand out across the LA/MS gulf coast. This ridge stays fairly \nstationary through the weekend with only a slight movement to just\noff the MA/ME coast line by Mon morning. This will but GA in more\nof an E to NE flow pattern and we could see a little bit of \nmoisture return across the area from the Atlantic going into next \nweek. As for now only expecting increased cloud cover across the \nstate days 5 through 7. This ridge does weaken a bit by Tue/Wed as\nan approaching low pressure system moves E out of the Central \nPlains. The main low center is expected to track across the \ncentral Great Lake states Wed and into the New England states Thu \nmorning. Its associated cold frontal boundary moves into NW GA \naround daybreak Wed and quickly sweeps through the state exiting \nthe GA coast by sunset. The good dynamics and moisture with the \nfront all push NE closer to the parent low center allowing this \ndry cold front to push through the SERN U.S. keeping things dry \nfor north and central GA.",
